 The MiSTer tape library: puts a tape image from the PDP2011 core's
 folder on the SD card (games/PDP2011 and its folders) on MT0:, as if
 you had chosen it in the OSD. MOUNT MT0: as usual after.

 Format:
     TLOAD name                 a .TAP or .TPC image, any folder
     TLOAD folder/name          ... from that folder (RSTS/V9.6/X.TAP)
     TLOAD                      what is on MT0:
     TLOAD/UNLOAD               empty the drive

 Case does not matter. If two folders have a tape of that name, TLOAD
 lists them and you give the folder. TDIR lists the library.

 TLOAD will not change a tape that is in use (mounted, allocated or
 assigned by any job, yours too): DISMOUNT, DEALLOCATE or DEASSIGN it
 first. It needs the MiSTer with MiSTer_pdp2011 and Host network not
 Off; elsewhere it says the library does not answer.
*Example
     $ TLOAD rsts_v9_6_install.tap
     Loaded RSTS/V9.6/rsts_v9_6_install.tap on MT0: (SIMH)
     $ MOUNT/FOREIGN MT0:
